WEBVTT

00:08.620 --> 00:11.990
Only one individual returned to their room

00:12.330 --> 00:14.510
before the late missus left for hers.

00:15.240 --> 00:17.460
Isn't that right...

00:17.460 --> 00:19.440
Detective Amamiya?

00:19.440 --> 00:22.630
Senpai? There's no way it was her.

00:22.630 --> 00:23.630
It wasn't.

00:25.390 --> 00:27.800
Amamiya-kun isn't the culprit.

00:28.450 --> 00:31.420
It was someone else who's 
here with us right now.

00:32.350 --> 00:33.840
What are you saying?

00:33.840 --> 00:36.330
She left first. That's a fact.

00:36.330 --> 00:38.030
I saw it, too.

00:38.030 --> 00:42.400
It's true that she's the only one 
with an uncertain alibi.

00:42.400 --> 00:47.940
But the simple act of creating 
this situation was impossible for her.

00:50.200 --> 00:54.380
And I can prove it to you right now.

00:58.460 --> 01:01.830
<i>To think my chance would come so quickly...</i>

01:02.680 --> 01:05.800
<i>Kamonohashi Ron, you don't know it,</i>

01:06.510 --> 01:11.810
<i>but I'm an instructor at the 
BLUE detective training academy.</i>

01:12.370 --> 01:17.280
<i>The moment I catch you sleuthing,
 that'll be the end of you!</i>

01:17.790 --> 01:18.800
At least,

01:19.770 --> 01:21.980
that's what Detective Isshiki says.

01:21.980 --> 01:22.940
Huh?

01:28.110 --> 01:29.760
<i>Asking a bit much, aren't we?!</i>

01:43.220 --> 01:46.540
Ron    Kamonohashi's

01:43.220 --> 01:46.540
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

03:00.950 --> 03:05.460
<b>#04   The Case of the Benizome Hot Spring Murder (Part 2)</b>

03:09.880 --> 03:12.590
Wait, hang on... Don't get carried away.

03:12.920 --> 03:17.110
Really, Detective Isshiki? 
We already have all the clues we need?

03:17.110 --> 03:18.550
Is that what you're saying?

03:18.550 --> 03:20.010
I—Wa—

03:20.010 --> 03:23.690
I see. "I" and "wa," you say?

03:24.200 --> 03:26.600
"I" for the illustration
of the secret story of Benizome,

03:26.600 --> 03:28.680
and "wa" for the water
turned red with leaves.

03:28.680 --> 03:30.910
Those are the keys to solving this mystery?

03:30.910 --> 03:35.490
By "secret story," you mean the one about 
the woman who was sacrificed, don't you?

03:35.490 --> 03:39.510
And that serves as proof 
that the lady detective is innocent?

03:39.510 --> 03:40.700
Apparently so.

03:41.190 --> 03:45.430
Oh, Amamiya-kun, you look bewildered.

03:45.830 --> 03:49.000
What's this story you keep talking about?

03:49.000 --> 03:52.120
It was in the pamphlet 
you got in the taxi, wasn't it?

03:52.120 --> 03:54.460
I didn't come by taxi.

03:54.460 --> 03:57.160
And I didn't see any
at the station when I arrived.

03:58.880 --> 04:01.850
Come to think of it,
I feel like you mentioned that before...

04:01.850 --> 04:04.560
That is, you came here on your own.

04:04.560 --> 04:07.770
I know exactly what 
Detective Isshiki is talking about.

04:09.100 --> 04:13.000
Work just wouldn't end, 
and I had to walk from the station.

04:13.000 --> 04:17.110
We made the pamphlet 
for the annex ourselves.

04:17.110 --> 04:18.850
I really am sorry.

04:20.820 --> 04:24.920
She had no opportunity to see the pamphlet. 
She didn't know the story.

04:24.920 --> 04:27.680
Therefore she couldn't commit
 a murder made to replicate it.

04:28.100 --> 04:30.950
In other words,
Amamiya-kun isn't the culprit.

04:30.950 --> 04:33.050
Detective Isshiki, you really are amazing.

04:33.050 --> 04:35.500
<i>I see now! Nice deduction!</i>

04:35.500 --> 04:41.220
That's true. The secret story wasn't written 
anywhere but that pamphlet from the taxi.

04:41.220 --> 04:47.930
It isn't a very pleasant story, 
so we don't tell it here at the inn.

04:49.780 --> 04:51.850
Then I guess it's as the detective says.

04:54.060 --> 04:56.530
<i>So it wasn't Kamonohashi Ron?</i>

04:56.530 --> 04:59.240
<i>It was Isshiki Totomaru who solved this?</i>

04:59.240 --> 05:01.550
Now, who's the real culprit?

05:01.550 --> 05:02.200
What?

05:02.200 --> 05:05.660
I don't know! You're the one 
who said it was someone here!

05:05.660 --> 05:08.260
What? So you haven't decided yet?

05:08.260 --> 05:10.800
Then I vote that it was a curse.

05:10.800 --> 05:12.120
You've gotta be kidding me.

05:12.120 --> 05:14.590
I saw something last night.

05:14.980 --> 05:18.050
I don't know about a curse,
but it certainly looked paranormal.

05:18.530 --> 05:19.260
What?

05:20.350 --> 05:24.890
After dinner, when I was going back 
to my room, I looked out at the river.

05:25.390 --> 05:28.260
There was a strange 
white mist rising from it.

05:28.940 --> 05:31.450
It was like some kind of spirit.

05:32.120 --> 05:33.800
A white mist?

05:33.800 --> 05:35.650
I found it, Toto!

05:35.650 --> 05:36.750
Look at the river!

05:36.750 --> 05:38.270
When'd you get over there?!

05:38.270 --> 05:39.560
You can see the mist?

05:39.560 --> 05:40.820
Of course not.

05:41.360 --> 05:42.280
Look!

05:42.280 --> 05:44.740
It's the ping-pong ball we lost last night.

05:44.740 --> 05:45.820
That was <i>your</i> fault!

05:45.820 --> 05:47.880
The heavy rain washed wood, leaves,

05:47.880 --> 05:49.630
and a gutter down the river.

05:49.630 --> 05:51.790
Add the ping-pong ball, and we've got a dam!

05:51.790 --> 05:55.860
Even if a beaver shows up now,
I want you to focus on the investigation!

05:56.750 --> 05:58.940
Is there anything we can use to get the ball?

05:58.940 --> 06:00.460
We can do that later!

06:01.190 --> 06:02.070
What's that?

06:02.070 --> 06:02.940
What?

06:03.750 --> 06:04.890
A bathmat?

06:04.890 --> 06:06.960
What's that doing out here?

06:06.960 --> 06:08.430
Think it could reach the ball?

06:08.430 --> 06:11.040
Enough about the ping-pong ball!

06:11.850 --> 06:13.330
Isshiki.

06:14.660 --> 06:16.520
<i>This is bad! She's pissed!</i>

06:17.070 --> 06:18.980
You really helped me out earlier.

06:20.570 --> 06:23.350
Thank y—

06:24.720 --> 06:27.280
<i>Her body physically refuses to thank me!</i>

06:28.530 --> 06:31.960
However, as long as any
 lingering doubt remains,

06:31.960 --> 06:35.100
I cannot lead the investigation.

06:35.100 --> 06:38.680
I am entrusting this case to you.

06:41.090 --> 06:43.800
Y-You are?

06:44.100 --> 06:45.610
You can count on me!

06:45.610 --> 06:47.050
Amamiya-senpai, I won't let you do—

06:47.050 --> 06:47.700
Shut up!

06:47.700 --> 06:48.470
Huh?!

06:48.470 --> 06:49.860
I don't expect anything from you!

06:49.860 --> 06:51.770
You're just the only one here!

06:51.770 --> 06:52.890
Sorry I misunderstood!

06:53.430 --> 06:55.860
This all just so unbelievable.

06:55.860 --> 06:59.190
Starting yesterday, when I walked
 into the wrong bath by accident...

06:59.190 --> 07:01.480
Yeah, that wasn't like you, Senpai.

07:04.370 --> 07:05.820
Amamiya-kun.

07:06.360 --> 07:08.030
Y-Yes?

07:08.030 --> 07:09.990
Excellent work.

07:09.990 --> 07:12.540
You weren't mistaken last night.

07:14.950 --> 07:17.670
S-Steaming hot...

07:17.670 --> 07:18.880
S-Steaming what?

07:18.880 --> 07:21.960
A superlatively steaming-hot hottie!

07:22.860 --> 07:25.420
You'd let <i>those</i> be your last words?!

07:28.110 --> 07:30.090
The police are here.

07:31.080 --> 07:32.430
Now then...

08:48.470 --> 08:49.940
Good job out there.

08:49.940 --> 08:50.880
Thanks.

08:50.880 --> 08:53.360
So, any new information?

08:53.360 --> 08:56.900
According to the medical exam, 
the cause of death was heart failure.

08:56.900 --> 09:01.930
According to her husband,
she had a long-standing heart condition.

09:02.280 --> 09:06.280
She'd have fits where she needed
 to be taken to the hospital.

09:08.220 --> 09:10.820
Did the coroner say anything else?

09:12.430 --> 09:17.290
<i>Go on, Kamonohashi Ron! Say something 
that proves you've been sleuthing!</i>

09:17.290 --> 09:19.540
There was also, let me think...

09:19.540 --> 09:21.000
Hey, there's a centipede on the wall.

09:24.770 --> 09:26.340
M-My ears!

09:28.150 --> 09:29.800
There's no centipede there.

09:30.150 --> 09:33.010
Of course not. I wouldn't kill a bug.

09:33.010 --> 09:35.420
Huh? What are you talking about?

09:35.420 --> 09:37.260
You nearly gave me a heart attack.

09:37.260 --> 09:38.600
Oh, right.

09:38.600 --> 09:42.500
They said the temperature difference between
 inside and outside caused the heart failure.

09:42.500 --> 09:44.100
It was thermal shock.

09:44.100 --> 09:45.660
I thought so.

09:45.660 --> 09:47.570
You did? You don't mean...

09:47.570 --> 09:49.780
Yes. All the pieces are in place.

09:50.310 --> 09:53.930
Detective Isshiki, you're up.

10:14.520 --> 10:16.500
What's going on?

10:16.500 --> 10:18.610
Has something else happened?

10:18.610 --> 10:21.120
Or is this about the incident before?

10:21.120 --> 10:24.710
Yes. It's about the late missus.

10:25.130 --> 10:27.650
With the blessing of the local police,

10:27.650 --> 10:30.150
I will now solve this case.

10:30.150 --> 10:32.860
You will? So you're saying...

10:32.860 --> 10:35.370
This was a murder.

10:35.370 --> 10:36.820
And...

10:37.220 --> 10:39.260
the murderer is here with us now.

10:42.740 --> 10:47.350
The murderer had to have known
that the victim had a weak heart.

10:47.800 --> 10:48.750
It's you, isn't it?

10:49.410 --> 10:50.520
Her husband.

10:53.660 --> 10:56.800
Wh-Why would I do that to my beloved wife?

10:56.800 --> 10:59.920
It's true that I knew about her condition.

10:59.920 --> 11:03.770
But of course I did. We're married.
There's nothing suspect about that, right?

11:03.770 --> 11:09.420
Besides, at the time of her death, 
I was with everyone else in the lounge.

11:09.420 --> 11:14.240
Indeed, you were with the rest
 of us in the lounge.

11:14.240 --> 11:16.450
Specifically so you'd have an alibi.

11:18.160 --> 11:22.160
Behind the scenes, you'd set a bold trap

11:22.160 --> 11:24.070
to lure your wife to her death.

11:24.070 --> 11:25.000
A trap?

11:25.000 --> 11:25.860
Yes.

11:34.780 --> 11:38.220
He left a bathmat like this, 
covering the entrance to the bath,

11:38.220 --> 11:40.180
to create a pitfall.

11:40.180 --> 11:44.290
Do you think we're stupid? 
No one would fall for—

11:42.760 --> 11:44.290
You're right.

11:44.290 --> 11:48.520
Under normal conditions, anyone could
 see through this trap quite easily.

11:48.520 --> 11:52.510
But without her glasses, 
the missus had very poor vision.

11:52.510 --> 11:54.440
Isn't that right, sir?

11:59.680 --> 12:03.580
Given her eyesight, this was more 
than enough to fool her.

12:05.790 --> 12:10.130
This trap made her fall into the bath,

12:10.740 --> 12:12.430
from whence she would never return.

12:15.050 --> 12:17.630
But she died of thermal shock, right?

12:17.630 --> 12:20.260
Is falling into bathwater 
really enough to stop a heart?

12:20.260 --> 12:23.560
Well, it's hard to imagine 
under normal circumstances.

12:23.560 --> 12:26.980
But what if the bath wasn't 
filled with warm water?

12:27.280 --> 12:29.190
What if it was freezing cold?

12:30.150 --> 12:30.980
What?

12:30.980 --> 12:32.060
Freezing water?

12:32.060 --> 12:33.770
This is a free-flowing hot spring!

12:33.770 --> 12:34.850
Ron.

12:34.850 --> 12:35.990
Okay.

12:46.910 --> 12:51.060
We found this discarded in the river.
This is how it was done.

12:51.060 --> 12:52.000
A rain gutter?

12:53.180 --> 12:57.610
Her husband knew there was an elevation
difference between the river and the bath.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.470
He made clever use of that.

12:59.470 --> 13:04.110
He used two rain gutters. One drew 
water from upstream into the bath.

13:04.110 --> 13:06.980
Then, by drawing the hot water 
from the bath into the river,

13:06.980 --> 13:09.430
he was able to create a freezing-cold spring.

13:09.430 --> 13:12.690
Then the white mist I saw last night was...

13:12.690 --> 13:13.890
That's right.

13:13.890 --> 13:16.110
It wasn't a paranormal phenomenon.

13:16.630 --> 13:20.480
It was steam from the hot bathwater
 hitting the cold river.

13:22.780 --> 13:25.170
There was just one hitch.

13:25.560 --> 13:30.200
All those fallen leaves in the river
from the heavy rains two days ago

13:30.200 --> 13:32.290
ended up in the hot spring.

13:33.060 --> 13:35.460
He couldn't pick out each and every one.

13:36.920 --> 13:40.330
So he decided to make use
 of the hidden legend.

13:40.710 --> 13:42.990
He gathered up even more fallen leaves

13:42.990 --> 13:46.790
and tried to make it look like 
the curse of the sacrificed woman,

13:46.790 --> 13:48.150
all to cover his tracks.

13:50.210 --> 13:53.350
That's enough! This is the women's bath!

13:53.350 --> 13:56.520
A man couldn't sneak in here
 long enough to set all that up!

13:56.520 --> 13:59.930
If you knew no one would be coming, 
that wouldn't be a problem.

14:00.700 --> 14:04.370
At dinner, you overheard 
that we'd be playing ping-pong,

14:04.370 --> 14:08.340
so you knew no one would be
 in the men's bath for a while.

14:08.870 --> 14:12.850
<b>Men</b>

14:08.870 --> 14:13.260
Then, by swapping the curtains
marking the men's and women's baths,

14:11.970 --> 14:17.840
<b>Women</b>

14:13.260 --> 14:15.340
you sent the ladies to the men's bath,

14:15.340 --> 14:17.840
ensuring you'd have 
the women's bath to yourself.

14:17.840 --> 14:20.430
Then the reason I went into the wrong one

14:20.430 --> 14:23.050
is because the signs had been swapped?

14:23.050 --> 14:24.280
That's right.

14:25.010 --> 14:30.220
Our ping-pong game ended 
much more quickly than he expected.

14:31.180 --> 14:34.610
So we went for a bath before 
he could swap the curtains back,

14:34.610 --> 14:37.440
and you walked in on us, Senpai.

14:37.440 --> 14:39.930
D-Do you have evidence of—

14:39.930 --> 14:42.660
If we test the curtain rods, 
we should still find

14:42.660 --> 14:45.110
your fingerprints, which 
have no reason to be there.

14:46.040 --> 14:49.170
You should have only 
been using the men's bath.

14:49.170 --> 14:52.580
So why would your prints be
 on the women's curtain rod?

14:52.580 --> 14:54.790
Can you explain that?

14:56.390 --> 14:57.790
That's...

15:00.780 --> 15:01.840
Checkmate.

15:03.000 --> 15:04.310
I got it all out.

15:07.970 --> 15:10.720
Michiyo, I failed.

15:11.210 --> 15:14.440
You can't be serious! You really killed her?

15:15.510 --> 15:17.540
But it was for you, Michiyo!

15:17.540 --> 15:19.730
What?! It's got nothing to do with me!

15:19.730 --> 15:20.640
Don't say that!

15:20.640 --> 15:23.740
You always said that she was in our way!

15:23.740 --> 15:25.800
I may have said, 
"If only your wife wasn't around!"

15:25.800 --> 15:27.870
But no one told you to go this far!

15:27.870 --> 15:32.650
You lowlife. 
To kill your wife over an affair...

15:32.650 --> 15:34.080
Michiyo!

15:34.080 --> 15:35.050
Let go of me!

15:34.080 --> 15:36.540
Don't abandon me, Michiyo!

15:35.050 --> 15:36.540
What were you thinking?

15:36.880 --> 15:39.000
You took your wife's life!

16:05.320 --> 16:06.570
Where's Ron?

16:09.160 --> 16:10.620
Huh? What's going on?!

16:14.560 --> 16:16.790
Ron? Ron!

16:17.440 --> 16:19.750
Over here, Isshiki Totomaru.

16:19.750 --> 16:20.610
Huh?

16:21.840 --> 16:24.550
This conversation will go faster
 with you here.

16:24.550 --> 16:26.030
You're from the inn.

16:26.510 --> 16:29.470
And it looks like he's just woken up.

16:32.630 --> 16:34.370
What did I do?

16:34.370 --> 16:36.830
I remember finding 
a black sugar syrup spring...

16:36.830 --> 16:38.140
That was a dream!

16:40.280 --> 16:42.110
Allow me to introduce myself.

16:42.940 --> 16:47.070
I am BLUE's tracking instructor, Spitz Fire.

16:47.070 --> 16:49.530
BLUE, as in the detective training school?

16:49.530 --> 16:53.630
I came to investigate whether 
Kamonohashi Ron was acting as a detective.

16:53.630 --> 16:56.400
To think they've got <i>you</i>
 for a tracking instructor...

16:56.400 --> 17:00.470
I spotted you all the way back at the 
shopping arcade where we did the raffle.

17:00.470 --> 17:01.750
What?

17:01.750 --> 17:04.790
You saw, didn't you? I didn't do a thing.

17:04.790 --> 17:07.460
Detective Isshiki cracked this case.

17:07.460 --> 17:09.140
Liar!

17:09.140 --> 17:12.060
A fool like Isshiki, 
who didn't even notice me,

17:12.060 --> 17:14.960
couldn't possibly make 
such brilliant deductions!

17:16.240 --> 17:18.140
<i>That was insightful, but it sure hurts.</i>

17:18.140 --> 17:19.850
What proof do you have?

17:19.850 --> 17:22.060
I don't care about proof!

17:22.060 --> 17:25.040
I know that those were your 
deductions, Kamonohashi Ron!

17:25.040 --> 17:29.280
So you aren't just bad at your specialty,
 shadowing and tailing,

17:29.280 --> 17:33.050
but you're also illogical.
I'm surprised you're an instructor at all.

17:33.050 --> 17:35.330
All that and this sham kidnapping...

17:35.330 --> 17:38.220
Are instructors just worse these days?

17:38.220 --> 17:39.750
Don't make him angry!

17:39.750 --> 17:42.700
He's right. It'd be best not to anger me.

17:42.700 --> 17:45.090
If you admit that you've been sleuthing,

17:45.090 --> 17:47.550
I can ask for a lighter sentence.

17:48.070 --> 17:50.510
Do you have the authority do to that?

17:51.970 --> 17:54.930
If you were only here 
to see if I'm sleuthing,

17:54.930 --> 17:58.970
you wouldn't need to disguise yourself
as a worker at the inn.

17:58.970 --> 18:03.190
But you went to the trouble of going 
undercover and interacting with us.

18:03.570 --> 18:08.430
If you were just here to observe,
that would be truly irrational.

18:08.430 --> 18:11.120
Not only are you 
exposing yourself to your target,

18:11.120 --> 18:14.660
there's always the possibility
that they might stymie you by fleeing.

18:15.200 --> 18:17.490
Given your earlier threat and your phrasing,

18:17.490 --> 18:20.100
plus your impatience, 
I sense something else at play.

18:20.100 --> 18:21.620
And it's a personal matter.

18:23.330 --> 18:26.700
You either made a bet 
with someone about me sleuthing,

18:26.700 --> 18:29.050
or you were threatened.

18:29.050 --> 18:30.580
Or, perhaps...

18:33.350 --> 18:36.250
you are in need of my abilities.

18:41.240 --> 18:44.060
I am utterly defeated. I'm no match for you.

18:44.410 --> 18:48.270
I guess I should have expected as much 
from BLUE's most brilliant student.

18:48.760 --> 18:51.670
I figured if I didn't do this, 
you'd never accept a job from me.

18:51.670 --> 18:52.700
A job?

18:53.060 --> 18:54.490
I knew it.

18:54.490 --> 18:56.700
Ron-kun! Please lend me your skills!

18:57.040 --> 18:58.110
What?

18:58.110 --> 19:01.100
I don't have outstanding deductive reasoning,

19:01.100 --> 19:05.580
so you might wonder why I honed my tracking 
skills to become an instructor at BLUE.

19:05.580 --> 19:10.300
It was all to find the best detective
to solve the mystery of my missing family.

19:10.300 --> 19:12.400
Your family is missing?

19:12.760 --> 19:16.520
But even at BLUE,
I couldn't find the right detective.

19:16.520 --> 19:20.950
When I asked, everyone said the same thing. 
"Maybe Kamonohashi Ron could..."

19:20.950 --> 19:25.090
Then came an order that afforded me
 this chance to meet you.

19:25.090 --> 19:30.480
And now I've confirmed that you're
 the detective I've been seeking, Ron-kun!

19:30.480 --> 19:31.690
I refuse.

19:31.690 --> 19:32.900
Why?!

19:32.900 --> 19:36.100
You're an instructor at BLUE, right?
 Who'd believe you?

19:36.100 --> 19:38.060
I don't even know you.

19:38.060 --> 19:40.620
A-Ah, yes. That's true.

19:40.910 --> 19:45.450
I suppose I just feel close to you
after investigating you so thoroughly.

19:45.450 --> 19:47.330
I'm a pretty good guy, though, you know?

19:47.330 --> 19:50.460
<i>Yeah. I'm sure he's a good, honest person.</i>

19:50.460 --> 19:51.290
Okay!

19:51.290 --> 19:53.500
I'm going to earn your trust!

19:53.500 --> 19:57.440
I'll go tell my superiors 
that you aren't doing detective work.

19:57.440 --> 19:59.390
You had better. Is that all?

19:59.390 --> 20:02.960
Huh? Oh, and I'll help you with 
your detective work, of course.

20:02.960 --> 20:04.970
I told you it's Detective Isshiki's work.

20:04.970 --> 20:08.440
R-Right. I'll help Detective Isshiki.

20:08.440 --> 20:09.920
Is that all?

20:09.920 --> 20:10.900
Huh?

20:10.900 --> 20:12.760
What? Um...

20:13.310 --> 20:16.030
I wanted to wear it around the house, but...

20:16.530 --> 20:17.670
Please take this happi coat!

20:17.670 --> 20:19.070
I didn't peg you for liking folksy stuff!

20:19.070 --> 20:20.780
It's too small for me.

20:20.780 --> 20:24.140
Come on now, Ron. 
He doesn't seem like a bad guy.

20:24.140 --> 20:26.000
Why don't you just hear him out?

20:27.030 --> 20:30.230
Tototo! I just knew you were the best!

20:30.230 --> 20:32.830
You're not smart, 
but you've got heart, Tototo!

20:32.830 --> 20:33.670
One too many "to"s.

20:34.710 --> 20:38.510
That last bit when you exposed 
the husband as the killer was good stuff.

20:41.090 --> 20:44.810
I'll leave for today, but if you ever 
need a tracker, just call me!

20:45.360 --> 20:47.660
I'll show you that I can win your trust!

20:50.480 --> 20:52.980
Okay, his exit was 
the biggest surprise of all!

20:53.350 --> 20:55.410
I hope he realizes no one actually agreed.

20:55.410 --> 20:57.190
So you're gonna turn him down?

20:57.530 --> 21:01.680
His skills would be helpful
in solving future mysteries,

21:01.680 --> 21:04.160
and I find his request intriguing.

21:04.160 --> 21:08.630
Still, as I can't completely trust him, 
I had planned to refuse him.

21:08.630 --> 21:09.650
Past tense?

21:10.120 --> 21:13.020
If he betrays me, I'm done for.

21:13.020 --> 21:16.120
But since you say he's a good guy, 
I'll wait and see.

21:16.120 --> 21:17.960
That's putting way too much on me!

21:17.960 --> 21:21.740
We just have to see 
if he's trustworthy or not.

21:21.740 --> 21:23.350
Do you have a plan?

21:23.350 --> 21:24.800
Of course.

21:24.800 --> 21:26.210
I'll use him till he drops.

21:26.210 --> 21:27.770
There's that demonic side!

21:28.120 --> 21:30.060
<i>Although whatever he might say,</i>

21:30.060 --> 21:33.480
<i>I've never seen Ron abandon 
someone who's in trouble.</i>

21:35.190 --> 21:39.650
Thanks for helping Amamiya-senpai 
in this murder case.

21:44.690 --> 21:47.040
I merely fulfilled my duty.
